/-!
# Quantitative current full-phase inputs from primitive frame data

`exists_finite_current_fullPhaseInputs` constructs a physically contained,
finite decorated frozen menu and actual `CarrierFullPhaseInput` objects for
the literal normalized determinant (`app:ch_seed:prop:seed-actual-menu`, Step 1).
Every positive full momentum/Fréchet comparison tolerance has a positive
componentwise frame `C⁶` threshold.

One family and one low neighborhood are fixed before all orders and accuracies.
`PatchQuantitativeFamily.current_phase_continuity_componentwise` gives phase
`C^m` continuity from componentwise frame `C^(m+1)` comparison, in particular
`C⁶ → C⁵`. `current_phase_bound` gives the sharp one-high frame order `m+1`;
the actual-carrier parent instantiates the projected-frame loss two to obtain
immersion order `m+3` (`app:ch_seed:eq:seed-phase-tame`).

The construction identifies the frozen benchmark by zero-error continuity and
root/ODE/inverse uniqueness. It chooses the common target before the final
patch shrinking and decorated cover. Doubled closed patch characteristicity,
annular and transverse bounds, centered incidence sections, detector data and
physical containment survive that refinement. The parent retains responsibility
for finite carrier, signed-pair, current incidence and detector assembly.
-/
